cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sahar: calibrating concept-emergence detection against documented origins"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bootwala
    given-names: Abbas
    affiliation: "The University of Texas at Dallas"
  - family-names: Malina
    given-names: Roger F.
    affiliation: "The University of Texas at Dallas"
abstract: >-
  Software for detecting when a concept enters a literature, and a protocol for
  measuring the error of that detection against origins documented outside the
  data. Includes two screens: one for terms carrying an older unrelated sense,
  and one for whether a concept can legitimately calibrate a given detector.
keywords:
  - scientometrics
  - novelty indicators
  - concept emergence
  - measurement error
  - validation
  - OpenAlex
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ABBASBOOTWALA/sahar"
